<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Reference//EN" "reference.dtd">
<reference id="api_player_setcanvas">
    <title><ph keyref="SetCanvas"/></title>
    <shortdesc id="short"><ph id="shortdesc" props="cpp">Sets the view window for displaying video.</ph><ph id="shortdesc" props="android">Sets the view window for displaying video.</ph><ph id="shortdesc" props="ios mac">Sets the view window for displaying the video.</ph></shortdesc>
    <prolog>
        <metadata>
            <keywords>
                <indexterm keyref="SetCanvas"/>
            </keywords>
        </metadata>
    </prolog>
    <refbody>
        <section id="prototype">
            <p outputclass="codeblock">
                <codeblock props="cpp" outputclass="language-cpp">bool SetCanvas(Canvas *canvas, Error *err = nullptr)</codeblock>
                <codeblock props="android" outputclass="language-java">public void setCanvas(Canvas canvas) throws RteException</codeblock>
            <codeblock props="ios mac" outputclass="language-objectivec">- (BOOL)setCanvas:(AgoraRteCanvas *_Nonnull)canvas error:(AgoraRteError * _Nullable)error;</codeblock>
            </p>
        </section>
        <section id="detailed_desc" deliveryTarget="details" otherprops="no-title">
            <dl outputclass="since">
                <dlentry props="cpp">
                    <dt>Since</dt>
                    <dd>Available since v4.4.0.</dd>
                </dlentry>
                <dlentry props="android">
                    <dt>Since</dt>
                    <dd>Available since v4.4.0.</dd>
                </dlentry>
            <dlentry props="ios mac">
                <dt>Since</dt>
                <dd>v4.5.0</dd>
            </dlentry>
            </dl>
            <p props="cpp">This method specifies a <xref keyref="Canvas"/> object to display video. Once the video stream starts playing successfully, the video will be displayed on this <xref keyref="Canvas"/>.</p>
            <p props="android">This method sets the <xref keyref="Canvas"/> object used to display video.</p>
        <p props="ios mac">This method specifies a Canvas object to display the video. Once the the video stream sucessfully plays, the video image will be displayed on the specified canvas.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="timing" deliveryTarget="details" props="android cpp">
            <title>Timing</title>
            <p props="cpp">This method must be called after <xref keyref="Player_Player"/> is called.</p>
            <p props="android">You must call this method after calling <xref keyref="Player_Player"/>.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="parameters" deliveryTarget="details" props="android cpp ios mac">
            <title>Parameters</title>
            <parml>
                <plentry props="cpp">
                    <pt>canvas</pt>
                    <pd><xref keyref="Canvas"/> object used to render video frames. See <xref keyref="Canvas"/>.</pd>
                </plentry>
                <plentry props="cpp">
                    <pt>err</pt>
                    <pd>Output parameter for status or error information. See <xref keyref="Error"/>.</pd>
                </plentry>
                <plentry props="android">
                    <pt>canvas</pt>
                    <pd>The object used to render video frames. See <xref keyref="Canvas"/>.</pd>
                </plentry>
            <plentry props="ios mac">
                <pt>canvas</pt>
                <pd>The Canvas object on which the video is rendered: <xref keyref="Canvas"/></pd>
            </plentry>
            <plentry props="ios mac" conkeyref="SetConfigs_Rte/err">
                <pt/>
                <pd/>
            </plentry>
            </parml>
        </section>
        <section id="exception" props="android">
            <title>Exceptions</title>
            <p props="android">When the method call fails, the SDK throws an exception and returns the corresponding error information. You need to catch and handle the exception.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="return_values" props="cpp ios mac">
            <title>Return Values</title>
            <p props="cpp">
                <ul>
                    <li><xref keyref="true"/>: Set successfully.</li>
                    <li><xref keyref="false"/>: Set failed. You can check the error code returned in the <codeph>err</codeph> parameter for details.</li>
                </ul>
            </p>
        <p props="ios mac">Whether the settings are successful:<ul>
                <li><codeph><ph keyref="true"/></codeph>: Yes.</li>
                <li><codeph><ph keyref="false"/></codeph>: No. Refer to the error code in <parmname props="cpp">err</parmname><parmname props="apple">error</parmname> to get the detaled information.</li>
                </ul></p>
            </section>
    </refbody>
</reference>
